Tier 4 -- policy against a fault-injecting mock adapter (workstation).

The full promotion ladder driven against a scripted mock that can return, per
call: success, failure, timeout, garbage, and empty output with a success
status -- the crashed-verifier lesson encoded as a test class. Every rung x
every outcome has an expected disposition, asserted as a truth table. See
TESTING.md §5.

Empty at M0: there is no ladder yet (M2) and no policy (M1).

Files named t_*.sh are tests; anything else here is ignored.
